WEBVTT

00:11.590 --> 00:12.630
(Enhanced Stamina, Enhanced Arm Strength)
The adventure streams that adventurers put on

00:12.630 --> 00:13.920
(Enhanced Leg Strength)
The adventure streams that adventurers put on

00:13.920 --> 00:16.500
are the most popular
content in the world now.

00:17.210 --> 00:19.390
You can watch livestreams...

00:19.730 --> 00:22.520
or you can watch edited versions
released as strategy guides.

00:22.890 --> 00:27.190
There are even some who host streams
about dungeon cooking or medicine-making.

00:27.740 --> 00:29.880
Streams are great publicity.

00:29.880 --> 00:32.490
They bring a flood of quests
to the more competent parties,

00:32.490 --> 00:36.900
and companies that want them to use
their products can sponsor them.

00:37.600 --> 00:39.160
Whoa, awesome!

00:39.160 --> 00:40.530
What the heck?

00:40.530 --> 00:44.050
He defeated a Steel Crab
without lifting a finger!

00:44.050 --> 00:46.190
I never knew you could fight this way.

00:46.190 --> 00:47.580
Hey, what's up?

00:47.580 --> 00:48.790
Check this out. It's wild.

01:01.720 --> 01:06.870
(I Left My A-Rank Party to Help My Former
Students Reach the Dungeon Depths)

02:22.020 --> 02:25.510
(Episode 2: A Forest Inhabited by Magic Beasts)

02:25.510 --> 02:27.730
(Episode 2: A Forest Inhabited by Magic Beasts)
So, my senior partymates,

02:27.730 --> 02:31.520
what did you think of this
new Clover member's exploits?

02:31.520 --> 02:34.440
How shall I say it?
It was on another level!

02:34.440 --> 02:37.400
Every part of it was so amazing,
I was beyond shocked!

02:37.400 --> 02:39.530
The food was delicious.

02:39.530 --> 02:41.910
Glad I could be of use.

02:41.910 --> 02:44.270
But isn't it awkward having
your former teacher,

02:44.270 --> 02:46.300
a guy of different rank and status,

02:46.300 --> 02:48.160
join your party out of nowhere?

02:48.160 --> 02:49.840
You're overthinking it.

02:49.840 --> 02:50.390
Am I?

02:50.390 --> 02:51.270
Yeah, you are!

02:51.270 --> 02:51.790
Yes.

02:52.060 --> 02:55.790
Oh, then we'll make you our party leader!

02:56.030 --> 02:56.670
Huh?

02:56.670 --> 03:01.090
Up until now, I was tentatively
serving as something like a leader,

03:01.090 --> 03:03.350
but we didn't have a proper one.

03:03.350 --> 03:05.550
Yeah, but... why me?

03:06.560 --> 03:07.060
Huh?

03:07.340 --> 03:11.060
You are our teacher, after all!

03:11.060 --> 03:13.690
The spirits must have guided you to us!

03:13.690 --> 03:16.290
B-But I've only been here for a day—

03:16.290 --> 03:19.200
I'm with her! I want you to do it!

03:19.200 --> 03:21.360
Yeah. You're very experienced.

03:21.360 --> 03:22.610
Come on, now...

03:22.940 --> 03:25.800
And Clover was basically
just formed today, right?

03:28.790 --> 03:30.160
The leader, huh?

03:30.160 --> 03:35.540
That might help me keep these kids safe
from the dangers we're bound to face.

03:35.990 --> 03:37.260
Okay, then.

03:37.260 --> 03:40.880
But if you ever think I'm not a
good enough leader, just tell me.

03:41.300 --> 03:42.280
Sweet!

03:42.280 --> 03:43.880
We appreciate it!

03:47.650 --> 03:50.720
(Aureus Royal Castle Ruins Labyrinth,
Fourth Floor)

03:50.780 --> 03:51.080
(Dile Wolves)

03:51.080 --> 03:54.640
(Dile Wolves)
Barry! More monsters coming from
the western corridor! I need you!

03:55.650 --> 03:57.900
Are you nuts?!
I've got my hands full here!

03:57.900 --> 03:59.760
They're gonna overrun us at this rate!

03:59.760 --> 04:01.580
Hey, newbie! Slow them down!

04:01.580 --> 04:03.650
What are you talking about?!
I can't do that!

04:03.650 --> 04:06.440
Damn it! Why are there so many?!

04:06.440 --> 04:09.910
I've never seen a pack of
Dile Wolves this big before!

04:10.240 --> 04:11.620
And they're too strong!

04:11.620 --> 04:14.960
Why'd you decide to come this far
down if that's all you've got?!

04:16.650 --> 04:17.330
Jamie!

04:21.050 --> 04:22.670
Camilla! Healing magic!

04:22.670 --> 04:24.420
I'm out of mana!

04:24.420 --> 04:25.930
You're kidding me!

04:27.450 --> 04:28.890
We gotta pull back!

04:34.710 --> 04:36.560
Jamie, are you okay?

04:37.100 --> 04:40.560
Camilla!
Can you use that healing magic yet?

04:40.560 --> 04:42.170
Where are the Mana Potions?

04:42.170 --> 04:43.740
I don't have any.

04:43.740 --> 04:46.570
The chore boy always provided them for me.

04:47.580 --> 04:48.660
Jamie!

04:48.660 --> 04:49.950
Any Healing Potions?

04:50.300 --> 04:54.200
Nope. That was the chore boy's job, too.

04:54.700 --> 04:56.720
Cork, do you have any?

04:58.790 --> 05:03.130
Look, I got this potion myself,
with my own money.

05:03.130 --> 05:05.170
I'm not obligated to give it to you.

05:05.170 --> 05:07.450
One of our members is on death's door!

05:07.450 --> 05:08.300
Hand it over!

05:08.300 --> 05:12.860
You told me when I joined that all members
are responsible for their own supplies.

05:12.860 --> 05:14.070
You'd better thank me.

05:14.070 --> 05:15.310
Camilla! Can you cast yet?!

05:16.200 --> 05:18.310
Just a little more...

05:18.310 --> 05:20.560
- Cheers!
- Good work today!

05:23.820 --> 05:26.820
Today was so much fun thanks to you, Yuke!

05:27.240 --> 05:30.140
I reported our quest completion
to the guild.

05:30.140 --> 05:33.270
The quest reward itself isn't much,

05:33.270 --> 05:35.990
but the Steel Crab was in good condition,

05:35.990 --> 05:37.580
so I sold it for a good price.

05:39.260 --> 05:42.590
Silk, how have you been
dividing up rewards up to now?

05:42.910 --> 05:45.290
I handled all our earnings myself.

05:45.290 --> 05:46.710
We used an allowance system.

05:47.030 --> 05:49.970
Really? It's unusual for someone
to handle all party expenses alone.

05:50.430 --> 05:54.660
We've been hoping to buy a place to
use as our party's base eventually.

05:54.660 --> 05:58.140
It doesn't feel right to
just stay in inns forever.

05:58.140 --> 06:00.850
So you've been saving up for that...

06:01.270 --> 06:04.450
We'll keep that the way
you've been doing it, then.

06:04.450 --> 06:06.480
Why don't we put everything
in a party vault?

06:06.780 --> 06:08.390
Let's do that, then.

06:08.390 --> 06:09.990
Are you sure that's all right, though?

06:09.990 --> 06:13.490
You don't have to change everything
just because I joined.

06:14.030 --> 06:18.370
We haven't been in trouble like
this since Thunder Pike formed.

06:18.370 --> 06:21.000
It's good that we were
able to save Jamie...

06:21.000 --> 06:25.000
but this all happened because
you're such a selfish coward!

06:25.270 --> 06:28.130
You said it. Talk about useless.

06:28.480 --> 06:30.880
We were in real trouble thanks to you.

06:31.570 --> 06:34.870
Dile Wolves are drawn to scents.

06:34.870 --> 06:39.540
You're supposed to use Beast Repellent
first if you're gonna dive into their den!

06:39.540 --> 06:43.400
If you knew that, why didn't
you have any ready for us?

06:43.400 --> 06:44.670
What?!

06:44.670 --> 06:48.650
We failed this quest because
of your lack of preparation.

06:49.020 --> 06:51.810
And you tried to blame
it on us when you forgot.

06:51.810 --> 06:53.160
Have you no shame?

06:53.160 --> 06:55.410
If you want to stay in this party—

06:55.910 --> 06:58.310
I didn't realize the great Thunder Pike

06:58.310 --> 07:02.450
was full of losers who didn't even
understand their own skill level!

07:02.450 --> 07:03.790
You can count me out!

07:04.070 --> 07:05.410
I won't put up with this!

07:06.160 --> 07:08.300
I feel like I've heard that line before...

07:08.680 --> 07:10.300
They're making a lot of noise over there.

07:10.300 --> 07:12.550
Have it your way, you useless idiot!

07:12.900 --> 07:14.550
What the heck are they doing?

07:14.870 --> 07:16.920
So what are we gonna do tomorrow?

07:16.920 --> 07:18.710
Let's do as Master said.

07:18.710 --> 07:20.230
For every quest we complete,

07:20.230 --> 07:22.060
we take two days off.

07:22.390 --> 07:25.190
Silk, you're calling me "Master" again.

07:25.810 --> 07:27.570
What are you gonna do, Yuke?

07:27.570 --> 07:32.110
Well... I guess I'll stock
up on supplies at the market.

07:32.110 --> 07:33.730
I'll buy scrolls and potions,

07:33.730 --> 07:37.580
and I'll make holy water with the
ashes we got from those Undead miners.

07:37.990 --> 07:40.450
That's right. You're an Alchemist.

07:40.450 --> 07:42.080
I'm a bit envious.

07:42.080 --> 07:46.210
Really? People always tell me Alchemists
don't make good adventurers.

07:48.430 --> 07:51.350
We'll meet up at the Adventurer's
Guild on the morning of the third day

07:51.350 --> 07:53.340
and decide what kind of job
we'll take next.

07:53.340 --> 07:54.220
Okay!

07:54.220 --> 07:57.260
This is the stream
everyone's watching today!

07:57.260 --> 07:58.600
Hey, it's Yuke!

07:58.600 --> 08:00.720
It got 5,500 views?!

08:00.720 --> 08:04.100
Huh? It's barely been half a
day since we streamed that.

08:04.100 --> 08:05.600
It has that many already?

08:05.600 --> 08:08.100
Man, isn't this amazing?

08:08.100 --> 08:09.940
What is he, a Red Mage?

08:09.940 --> 08:13.660
He destroyed the Steel Crab, the Novice
Slayer of the Paintal Abandoned Mine Dungeon,

08:13.660 --> 08:16.360
without ever even touching it!

08:16.360 --> 08:19.340
Wow, he beat it with just weakening magic.

08:19.340 --> 08:20.160
For real?

08:20.160 --> 08:21.990
A new party, huh?

08:22.300 --> 08:25.380
It had over 6,000 views by the end!

08:25.380 --> 08:26.620
You really are amazing!

08:26.620 --> 08:29.750
The Steel Crab trips a lot of people up.

08:29.750 --> 08:31.880
Maybe a lot of newbies were watching.

08:31.880 --> 08:33.670
It won't help them any!

08:33.670 --> 08:35.130
You're just too strong!

08:35.500 --> 08:36.650
(Paralyze, Slow, Venom, Blindness, Collapse)
Who knew someone with an obscure job
like Red Mage could fight like that?!

08:36.650 --> 08:39.430
Who knew someone with an obscure job
like Red Mage could fight like that?!

08:39.430 --> 08:41.890
The streaming party's called Clover!

08:41.890 --> 08:45.340
Clover might just send a new
breeze blowing through the world!

08:45.340 --> 08:47.210
Keep your eyes on these guys!

08:47.210 --> 08:50.050
And that concludes our
"Highlight of the Day" stream!

08:50.050 --> 08:50.770
Meow!

08:51.140 --> 08:54.570
Huh? Looks like
Yuke's getting kinda cocky.

08:54.570 --> 08:56.280
"Clover," was it?

08:56.570 --> 08:58.980
Hmph! That useless idiot.

08:58.980 --> 09:01.780
Joining a low-ranked party
is giving him a big head.

09:02.150 --> 09:03.660
Let's celebrate.

09:03.660 --> 09:07.190
We do have a whole lot to celebrate today!

09:07.190 --> 09:09.040
All thanks to you, Yuke!

09:09.890 --> 09:11.050
Yuke?

09:11.050 --> 09:15.580
O-Oh, nothing. Come on,
let's have another toast.

09:15.580 --> 09:16.550
To Clover!

09:17.170 --> 09:18.680
To Clover!

09:20.070 --> 09:22.350
Master, are you crying?

09:22.350 --> 09:23.330
Of course not!

09:23.330 --> 09:24.630
Wanna go somewhere else?

09:24.630 --> 09:29.020
Who does he think he is,
getting all cozy like that?

09:36.250 --> 09:37.990
Is something the matter?

09:37.990 --> 09:40.950
Just wondering what might provide
good experience for three newbies

09:40.950 --> 09:44.540
while also being worth a high
score and a decent reward.

09:44.540 --> 09:46.910
That's getting a bit greedy.

09:46.910 --> 09:52.920
Experience aside, I think the girls in  Clover
have the skills to handle B-rank quests.

09:52.920 --> 09:55.420
How about this quest, then?

09:55.780 --> 09:57.560
A C-rank quest...

09:57.560 --> 10:00.330
"Fetch three stones from
the Yomun Waterfall."

10:01.160 --> 10:03.270
Why is this a C-rank quest?

10:03.270 --> 10:06.060
It seems easy enough to be D-rank at most.

10:06.700 --> 10:09.030
So if it's C-rank, does that mean...

10:09.030 --> 10:11.560
something's off
in the Ordan Lakeside Forest?

10:12.050 --> 10:15.440
Yes. It seems a large magic beast
has taken up residence there.

10:16.550 --> 10:18.010
What will it be?

10:18.010 --> 10:19.510
A magic beast, huh?

10:19.510 --> 10:23.270
It's dangerous, but this would
normally be a D-rank job,

10:23.270 --> 10:25.750
so if it would earn them
C-rank scores and rewards...

10:25.750 --> 10:26.950
Morning, Yuke!

10:27.380 --> 10:28.340
Morning.

10:28.340 --> 10:29.580
Good morning!

10:29.960 --> 10:32.600
Morning, you three. Perfect timing.

10:32.600 --> 10:35.670
There's a quest to fetch stones from the
Yomun Waterfall in the Ordan Lakeside Fo—

10:35.670 --> 10:37.070
Okay, let's do it!

10:37.070 --> 10:39.090
Uh, I'm not done explaining it yet.

10:39.090 --> 10:41.600
If Yuke says we can do it,
it's fine, right?

10:41.600 --> 10:45.020
Indeed. He's our leader now, after all.

10:45.020 --> 10:46.100
No objections.

10:46.410 --> 10:47.600
Well, then...

10:50.420 --> 10:52.550
I'll go process your
acceptance of this quest.

10:53.480 --> 10:56.230
Hang on! Are you sure about this?

10:56.500 --> 11:00.720
Sure! We've been to the Ordan
Lakeside Forest before.

11:00.720 --> 11:02.740
Why is it C-rank, though?

11:02.740 --> 11:06.150
I did tell you I wasn't
done explaining it yet.

11:06.150 --> 11:08.740
It seems a magic beast has
been showing up there lately.

11:09.070 --> 11:10.300
A magic beast?!

11:10.300 --> 11:12.360
There's still time to cancel that quest.

11:12.360 --> 11:15.380
No, we want the score. We'll do it.

11:15.850 --> 11:18.250
We're fine as long as we have you.

11:18.560 --> 11:22.030
All right. Go get ready, then.

11:22.030 --> 11:24.260
We'll meet at the stagecoach stop
in an hour.

11:24.500 --> 11:25.160
Okay.

11:25.160 --> 11:27.790
Got it! We'll be as quick as possible!

11:30.010 --> 11:32.390
Here's your quest acceptance receipt.

11:32.390 --> 11:33.990
Good luck.

11:33.990 --> 11:37.650
Did you arrange things so
that we'd accept this quest?

11:38.670 --> 11:43.090
That Clover stream got over
10,000 views, you know.

11:43.090 --> 11:46.280
People are clamoring to
catch their next stream.

11:46.730 --> 11:48.380
Well, that's awkward...

11:48.380 --> 11:50.620
Maybe I drew the wrong
kind of attention to us...

11:50.990 --> 11:52.970
I'm looking forward to it myself.

11:52.970 --> 11:54.750
You're talking like that, too?

11:56.430 --> 11:59.830
But I'll stream it to bring
some attention to those girls.

11:59.830 --> 12:03.380
And finding out what the magic beast
is will benefit the guild, right?

12:03.660 --> 12:07.110
Yes, but remember to uphold the
established dungeon work procedures,

12:07.110 --> 12:08.890
and don't try to do
more than you can handle.

12:19.510 --> 12:21.680
Pretty sloppy tailing work.

12:21.680 --> 12:24.450
He doesn't seem to be any kind of thief...

12:31.380 --> 12:33.460
I should be far enough away now.

12:33.460 --> 12:35.670
You're Yuke, aren't you?!

12:35.670 --> 12:36.330
No.

12:36.330 --> 12:37.580
Don't lie to me!

12:38.380 --> 12:42.710
If you were stalking me knowing
who I was, then don't ask.

12:42.710 --> 12:44.840
So? Do you have business with me?

12:45.140 --> 12:47.340
Leave Clover!

12:47.340 --> 12:50.430
Leave the party I just joined
three days ago?

12:50.430 --> 12:52.450
I'm afraid I can't do that.

12:52.450 --> 12:55.100
I'm the leader of Clover, you know.

12:55.100 --> 12:57.480
The leader? You?!

12:57.480 --> 12:58.850
Get real!

12:59.130 --> 12:59.980
Snare.

13:01.190 --> 13:06.860
I should be first! I told them a million
times that I'd join that party for them!

13:06.860 --> 13:08.180
"For them"?

13:08.180 --> 13:11.200
I found them first! Back off!

13:11.200 --> 13:12.590
Are you drunk?

13:12.590 --> 13:15.080
Or did you take some illegal potion?

13:15.080 --> 13:18.960
Shut up! If you don't wanna get hurt,
say you'll leave that party right now!

13:18.960 --> 13:22.780
I get what you're saying,
but my answer is no.

13:23.460 --> 13:25.210
You worthless newbie!

13:25.210 --> 13:26.720
I hope you're ready for pain!

13:29.360 --> 13:33.500
I was right to cast Snare the
moment he drew his sword.

13:33.500 --> 13:36.230
Really, what a troublesome drunk.

13:39.850 --> 13:42.020
That was a man named Besio Salas.

13:42.020 --> 13:45.240
He's offered to join our party countless
times at the Adventurer's Guild,

13:45.240 --> 13:47.560
as if it'd be a favor to us.

13:47.560 --> 13:49.140
He won't take no for an answer.

13:49.140 --> 13:50.540
It's been quite a problem.

13:51.310 --> 13:56.250
For all his bluster, his skills
really weren't all that special.

13:56.250 --> 13:59.450
Well, given he's dumb enough to draw
his sword in the middle of town...

13:59.450 --> 14:02.030
You aren't hurt, are you?

14:02.030 --> 14:03.280
I'm just fine.

14:03.280 --> 14:05.250
I left him unconscious on the street.

14:05.600 --> 14:06.880
Oh, good.

14:07.340 --> 14:10.510
I'm sorry you had to go
through that because of us.

14:10.880 --> 14:12.580
It's not your fault.

14:12.580 --> 14:15.480
I'll report him to the
guild when we get back,

14:15.480 --> 14:18.140
and if he comes around again,
I'll deal with him.

14:18.140 --> 14:20.770
Yuke! We can always count on you!

14:20.770 --> 14:23.470
Now, now. Flatter me all you want, but...

14:23.470 --> 14:24.870
all I'll give you is candy.

14:24.870 --> 14:26.400
But you do have candy.

14:27.650 --> 14:28.900
He really does...

14:31.420 --> 14:33.160
Okay, let's switch gears.

14:33.630 --> 14:35.860
We should review our quest first.

14:35.860 --> 14:39.570
Our objective is to fetch three
stones from the Yomun Waterfall.

14:39.570 --> 14:42.540
We can do that easily as soon as
we get to the lake at its foot.

14:42.540 --> 14:44.540
The problem is the magic beast.

14:45.600 --> 14:48.120
Since it lives in a forested region,

14:48.120 --> 14:53.050
it's probably something like
a bear, deer, wolf, or boar.

14:53.450 --> 14:56.640
You said you've been to the Ordan
Lakeside Forest before, right?

14:56.640 --> 14:59.800
Yeah. About two months ago, I think?

14:59.800 --> 15:01.540
Did you run into any monsters?

15:02.220 --> 15:03.460
We didn't, right?

15:03.460 --> 15:06.100
There weren't even any
regular animals around.

15:07.610 --> 15:08.770
Yuke?

15:08.770 --> 15:12.990
The Ordan Lakeside Forest was
always teeming with wildlife.

15:12.990 --> 15:13.820
You mean...

15:14.310 --> 15:16.640
You avoided encountering it
out of pure luck,

15:16.640 --> 15:20.200
but the magic beast was already
in the forest at that time.

15:21.670 --> 15:24.460
When we enter the forest, I'll
release my Camerat and start recording.

15:25.050 --> 15:28.760
If we find the magic beast and enter
combat, we'll start livestreaming

15:28.760 --> 15:30.560
and defeat it if we can.

15:30.560 --> 15:32.590
Even if we flee,
I want to get it on video.

15:32.590 --> 15:34.840
Why livestream it?

15:35.260 --> 15:37.900
The goal is to identify what
type of magic beast it is.

15:37.900 --> 15:41.220
And if we get into trouble
while the stream is live,

15:41.220 --> 15:44.870
the guild will be watching,
so they're likely to send backup.

15:44.870 --> 15:47.320
And if we manage to
defeat the magic beast,

15:47.320 --> 15:48.860
it'll prove we finished it off.

15:48.860 --> 15:52.270
It never occurred to me that you
could use livestreams that way.

15:52.270 --> 15:55.240
So this is finally our streaming debut!

15:56.120 --> 15:58.870
I should've bought clothes that
would look better on camera...

15:59.250 --> 16:01.000
You're more into this than I expected.

16:01.310 --> 16:04.120
I-Is my hair all right like this?

16:04.120 --> 16:05.580
Does it look strange?

16:05.580 --> 16:09.970
Aw, she has the same cute
side as any girl that age.

16:09.970 --> 16:14.840
Wait... Does "a girl that age" mean
the same thing for a dark elf?

16:14.840 --> 16:16.940
Don't worry, Yuke!

16:16.940 --> 16:19.050
Silk is definitely 17!

16:19.050 --> 16:20.350
She's not an old lady!

16:20.350 --> 16:22.470
Huh?! I didn't say anything!

16:22.770 --> 16:26.020
Don't give away my age
without my permission!

16:26.020 --> 16:30.360
And Master, it's improper
to question a lady's age!

16:30.720 --> 16:32.960
But I didn't say anything...

16:34.970 --> 16:37.990
Just so you know, I'm the oldest.

16:37.990 --> 16:38.870
I'm 20.

16:38.870 --> 16:40.540
Uh, I didn't as—

16:40.540 --> 16:42.550
What? Really?

16:42.550 --> 16:44.370
I wouldn't have guessed you're my age...

16:44.850 --> 16:46.880
You certainly don't look it.

16:47.880 --> 16:50.380
Wait, no! I wasn't looking!
You've got it all wrong!

16:50.380 --> 16:51.970
Don't do that, Yuke!

16:51.970 --> 16:53.360
She's self-conscious!

16:53.360 --> 16:54.390
I told you, I wasn't!

16:54.390 --> 16:55.170
(Ordan Lakeside Forest)
I told you, I wasn't!

16:55.170 --> 16:57.140
(Ordan Lakeside Forest)

17:00.100 --> 17:03.520
Okay, stay alert from this point on.

17:03.990 --> 17:07.430
If any newbie adventurers other
than us had accepted this quest,

17:07.430 --> 17:09.280
wouldn't they be in danger?

17:09.750 --> 17:12.400
I think that's why she told me about it.

17:13.040 --> 17:15.650
Mamar is pretty on the ball
about that kind of thing.

17:15.940 --> 17:17.080
I see.

17:17.080 --> 17:19.830
If things get dicey, withdraw right away.

17:19.830 --> 17:20.630
Got it?

17:24.690 --> 17:28.040
Okay, let's have fun, but be careful.

17:28.040 --> 17:29.730
Recording started.

17:35.650 --> 17:37.430
No sign of any animals...

17:38.000 --> 17:39.930
It's definitely here.

17:39.930 --> 17:42.170
Sh-Should I be in the lead?

17:42.170 --> 17:44.490
This is the opposite of
what we did in the dungeon.

17:44.490 --> 17:47.070
There probably aren't
any traps in the forest.

17:47.070 --> 17:51.250
Also, beasts tend to attack from behind.

17:51.250 --> 17:54.190
Since I can use Blink Shadow,
I should bring up the rear.

17:54.190 --> 17:57.190
But doesn't that put you in danger?

17:57.570 --> 18:00.690
I'm wearing magic armor
I found in a dungeon.

18:00.690 --> 18:03.080
I won't die that easily.

18:03.080 --> 18:05.450
So it really is Warlock Attire!

18:05.450 --> 18:07.160
Is that a big deal?

18:07.160 --> 18:07.170
It has high defense, it amplifies magic,

18:07.170 --> 18:10.640
(Warlock Attire)
It has high defense, it amplifies magic,

18:10.640 --> 18:14.170
it can assist, and it even replenishes mana.
(Warlock Attire)

18:14.170 --> 18:18.710
Uh, so in other words, it's okay
to have Yuke bring up the rear?

18:18.710 --> 18:20.050
Exactly.

18:25.400 --> 18:27.340
Master, that sound...

18:28.010 --> 18:29.900
The Yomun Waterfall is close.

18:29.900 --> 18:31.810
I hope we get there without incident.

18:33.490 --> 18:34.820
I see it. That's the Yomun Waterfall.

18:36.020 --> 18:37.280
Stop!

18:37.840 --> 18:40.160
Camerat, livestream mode!

18:40.160 --> 18:41.660
Understood.

18:46.800 --> 18:47.320
(Magic Beast Zarnag)

18:47.320 --> 18:48.710
(Magic Beast Zarnag)
A Zarnag?!

18:48.710 --> 18:50.550
(Magic Beast Zarnag)
That's a high-ranked monster that normally

18:50.550 --> 18:53.670
(Magic Beast Zarnag)
lives in the northern wastelands
or the deepest dungeon levels!

18:53.670 --> 18:55.040
It's the Beast King of the Far North!

18:56.460 --> 18:59.170
It's not normal for a monster
like this to appear in Ordan!

18:59.490 --> 19:03.180
Clover's nowhere near strong
enough to take this thing on!

19:03.550 --> 19:05.850
What is a monster like that doing here?

19:05.850 --> 19:08.090
Listen! I'll keep it here!

19:08.090 --> 19:09.310
Fall back right now!

19:09.760 --> 19:12.870
The guild should know from our
live stream what the situation is!

19:12.870 --> 19:14.770
They'll put out an emergency quest!

19:14.770 --> 19:17.830
Silk, you'll be the leader in my place.

19:17.830 --> 19:20.280
Make the members' safety
your top priority.

19:23.520 --> 19:25.870
It's still waiting to see what we'll do.

19:25.870 --> 19:26.900
Go while you can!

19:26.900 --> 19:28.690
I won't do that!

19:28.690 --> 19:30.960
Yuke, you can hold it in place, right?

19:30.960 --> 19:33.670
If I cut off its head
while you do that, we win!

19:35.340 --> 19:38.040
It's the biggest, so it's ours!

19:38.040 --> 19:39.170
Resounding thunder...

19:39.590 --> 19:42.170
As long as we're in a forest,
I can slow it down, too!

19:42.480 --> 19:45.180
You guys... This thing
is seriously dangerous!

19:45.180 --> 19:47.600
It's dangerous for you, too!

19:48.150 --> 19:50.180
All right. Let's do it!

19:50.540 --> 19:51.680
As Clover!

19:52.450 --> 19:53.690
Physical Enchant!

19:53.690 --> 19:53.700
...grant me great power!

19:53.700 --> 19:55.560
(Enhanced Arm Strength,
Enhanced Leg Strength, Enhanced Stamina)
...grant me great power!

19:56.380 --> 19:58.110
Scourge of light...

20:07.030 --> 20:07.660
Marina!

20:08.580 --> 20:09.450
Shock!

20:09.670 --> 20:10.340
(Shock)

20:10.660 --> 20:11.580
Paralyze!

20:11.580 --> 20:15.080
Slow! Venom! Collapse! Blindness!

20:15.840 --> 20:19.300
(Collapse, Slow,
Blindness, Venom, Paralyze)

20:22.810 --> 20:24.180
It didn't do much at all...

20:25.170 --> 20:27.640
Is it a Special Being? A Named?

20:28.790 --> 20:31.270
Sorry, Yuke! I can keep going!

20:33.230 --> 20:34.360
Don't hesitate!

20:34.360 --> 20:37.650
That magic is the only thing
that can get us out of this!

20:38.000 --> 20:39.860
Marina! Can you buy me time?

20:39.860 --> 20:40.860
Even a little will do!

20:40.860 --> 20:42.150
Got it!

20:47.520 --> 20:49.410
Scent of decaying roses...

20:55.760 --> 20:57.960
I've requested the aid of the dryads!

20:58.290 --> 21:01.710
Sea that swallows the light of the
setting sun as the black dog howls...

21:07.610 --> 21:11.470
With the mingling of black and
white, souls vanish into chaos!

21:11.470 --> 21:12.720
Get back, Marina!

21:13.740 --> 21:16.350
Take this! Grade 5 Magic:

21:17.850 --> 21:19.860
Prismatic Missile!

22:56.040 --> 22:56.560
(Overflow)

22:56.560 --> 22:58.680
Next time, "Overflow."

22:58.680 --> 23:01.050
(Overflow)
